{"id":"mahabharata-12-270","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":270,"title":"सप्तत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 270 · Vritra and Ushanas","summary":{"en":"Vritra, defeated by the gods, asks the sage Ushanas, the preceptor of the asuras, how it is that he is not afflicted, and why the asuras are in distress. Ushanas answers the angry words of the asuras and begins teaching the king Vritra.","kn":"ದೇವತೆಗಳಿಂದ ಸೋತ ವೃತ್ರ ತನ್ನನ್ನು ಏಕೆ ಪೀಡಿಸುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಅಸುರರೇಕೆ ಸಂಕಟದಲ್ಲಿದ್ದಾರೆಂದು ಅಸುರಗುರು ಉಶನಸನನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಉಶನಸ ಅಸುರರ ಕೋಪದ ಮಾತಿಗೆ ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ ರಾಜ ವೃತ್ರನಿಗೆ ಬೋಧನೆ ಆರಂಭಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"देवताओं से हारा वृत्र असुरगुरु उशना से पूछता है कि वे क्यों व्यथित नहीं और असुर क्यों संकट में हैं। उशना असुरों के क्रोधित वचनों का उत्तर देकर राजा वृत्र को उपदेश आरम्भ करते हैं।","te":"దేవతల చేత ఓడిన వృత్రుడు అసుర గురువు ఉశనసుని తాను ఎందుకు బాధపడడు, అసురులు ఎందుకు సంకటంలో ఉన్నారని అడుగుతాడు. ఉశనసుడు అసురుల కోపపు మాటలకు బదులిచ్చి రాజు వృత్రునికి బోధన ప్రారంభిస్తాడు.","ta":"தேவர்களிடம் தோற்ற வித்ரன் அசுர குரு உசனஸிடம் அசுரர் ஏன் துயரில் உள்ளனர் என்று கேட்கிறான். உசனஸ் அசுரர்களின் சினமிகு சொற்களுக்குப் பதிலளித்து மன்னன் வித்ரனுக்குப் போதனை தொடங்குகிறார்.","ml":"ദേവന്മാരാൽ പരാജയപ്പെട്ട വൃത്രൻ, അസുരന്മാരുടെ ഗുരുവായ ഉശനസ്സ് മുനിയോട് തനിക്ക് ദുഃഖമില്ലാത്തത് എന്തുകൊണ്ടെന്നും അസുരന്മാർ ദുരിതത്തിലായത് എന്തുകൊണ്ടെന്നും ചോദിക്കുന്നു. കോപിച്ച അസുരന്മാരുടെ വാക്കുകൾക്ക് ഉശനസ്സ് മറുപടി നൽകുകയും, രാജാവായ വൃത്രനെ പഠിപ്പിക്കാൻ തുടങ്ങുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.270; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"धन्या धन्या इति जनाः सर्वेऽस्मान्प्रवदन्त्युत ।\nन दुःखिततरः कश्चित्पुमानस्माभिरस्ति ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"All people call us fortunate, fortunate; yet there is no man more sorrowful than we."}},{"n":2,"text":"लोकसंभावितैर्दुःखं यत्प्राप्तं कुरुसत्तम ।\nप्राप्य जातिं मनुष्येषु देवैरपि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Kurus, the sorrow that even gods, honored by the world, have met on gaining birth among men, we have met."}},{"n":3,"text":"कदा वयं करिष्यामः संन्यासं दुःखसंज्ञकम् ।\nदुःखमेतच्छरीराणां धारणं कुरुसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"When shall we practice renunciation, which is called sorrow? Bearing these bodies is sorrow, best of the Kurus."}},{"n":4,"text":"विमुक्ताः सप्तदशभिर्हेतुभूतैश्च पञ्चभिः ।\nइन्द्रियार्थैर्गुणैश्चैव अष्टाभिः प्रपितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great-grandfather, freed from the seventeen, the five causal elements, the objects of the senses and the eight qualities,"}},{"n":5,"text":"न गच्छन्ति पुनर्भावं मुनयः संशितव्रताः ।\nकदा वयं भविष्यामो राज्यं हित्वा परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"sages of firm vows do not go again to rebirth. When shall we be so, giving up the kingdom, scorcher of foes?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"नास्त्यनन्तं महाराज सर्वं संख्यानगोचरम् ।\nपुनर्भावोऽपि संख्यातो नास्ति किंचिदिहाचलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nothing is endless, great king; everything falls within counting. Even rebirth is counted; nothing here is fixed."}},{"n":7,"text":"न चापि गम्यते राजन्नैष दोषः प्रसङ्गतः ।\nउद्योगादेव धर्मज्ञ कालेनैव गमिष्यथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"And it is not gone through by mere continuance; this is no fault of the connection. Through effort alone, knower of dharma, you will go in time."}},{"n":8,"text":"ईशोऽयं सततं देही नृपते पुण्यपापयोः ।\nतत एव समुत्थेन तमसा रुध्यतेऽपि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"This embodied one is always master of merit and demerit, king; yet by the darkness that rises from that very source he is also bound."}},{"n":9,"text":"यथाञ्जनमयो वायुः पुनर्मानःशिलं रजः ।\nअनुप्रविश्य तद्वर्णो दृश्यते रञ्जयन्दिशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As air carrying collyrium, or red arsenic, or dust, entering a place shows its color, tinting the quarters,"}},{"n":10,"text":"तथा कर्मफलैर्देही रञ्जितस्तमसावृतः ।\nविवर्णो वर्णमाश्रित्य देहेषु परिवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"so the embodied, tinted by the fruits of action and covered in darkness, though colorless takes on color and turns about in bodies."}},{"n":11,"text":"ज्ञानेन हि यदा जन्तुरज्ञानप्रभवं तमः ।\nव्यपोहति तदा ब्रह्म प्रकाशेत सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When by knowledge a creature drives off the darkness born of ignorance, then the eternal Brahman shines forth."}},{"n":12,"text":"अयत्नसाध्यं मुनयो वदन्ति\nये चापि मुक्तास्त उपासितव्याः ।\nत्वया च लोकेन च सामरेण\nतस्मान्न शाम्यन्ति महर्षिसंघाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sages say it is not won by effort; and those who are liberated are to be honored by you and by the world with its gods; therefore the hosts of great sages do not become quiet."}},{"n":13,"text":"अस्मिन्नर्थे पुरा गीतं शृणुष्वैकमना नृप ।\nयथा दैत्येन वृत्रेण भ्रष्टैश्वर्येण चेष्टितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this matter, hear with one mind, king, what was sung long ago, how the demon Vritra acted when he had fallen from his lordship."}},{"n":14,"text":"निर्जितेनासहायेन हृतराज्येन भारत ।\nअशोचता शत्रुमध्ये बुद्धिमास्थाय केवलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Defeated, without allies, robbed of his kingdom, Bharata, he did not grieve among his enemies, relying on understanding alone."}},{"n":15,"text":"भ्रष्टैश्वर्यं पुरा वृत्रमुशना वाक्यमब्रवीत् ।\nकच्चित्पराजितस्याद्य न व्यथा तेऽस्ति दानव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ushanas once spoke to Vritra, fallen from power: \"Danava, I hope you feel no pain at having been defeated now?\""}},{"text":"वृत्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vritra said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"सत्येन तपसा चैव विदित्वा संक्षयं ह्यहम् ।\nन शोचामि न हृष्यामि भूतानामागतिं गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By truth and austerity I have known the destruction of things, so I neither grieve nor rejoice at the coming and going of beings."}},{"n":17,"text":"कालसंचोदिता जीवा मज्जन्ति नरकेऽवशाः ।\nपरिदृष्टानि सर्वाणि दिव्यान्याहुर्मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Impelled by Time, helpless creatures sink in hell; the wise say all these have been seen to be divine."}},{"n":18,"text":"क्षपयित्वा तु तं कालं गणितं कालचोदिताः ।\nसावशेषेण कालेन संभवन्ति पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having used up the time reckoned for them, driven by Time, they are born again and again with the remaining time."}},{"n":19,"text":"तिर्यग्योनिसहस्राणि गत्वा नरकमेव च ।\nनिर्गच्छन्त्यवशा जीवाः कालबन्धनबन्धनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After going through thousands of animal births and hell too, helpless creatures come out, bound by the bonds of Time."}},{"n":20,"text":"एवं संसरमाणानि जीवान्यहमदृष्टवान् ।\nयथा कर्म तथा लाभ इति शास्त्रनिदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus I have seen creatures wandering. \"As the deed, so the gain\" is the scripture's teaching."}},{"n":21,"text":"तिर्यग्गच्छन्ति नरकं मानुष्यं दैवमेव च ।\nसुखदुःखे प्रियद्वेष्ये चरित्वा पूर्वमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"They go to animal births, to hell, to human and to divine states, having first known pleasure and pain, liking and dislike."}},{"n":22,"text":"कृतान्तविधिसंयुक्तं सर्वलोकः प्रपद्यते ।\nगतं गच्छन्ति चाध्वानं सर्वभूतानि सर्वदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whole world goes by the order of fate; all beings always go the road already traveled."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"कालसंख्यानसंख्यातं सृष्टिस्थितिपरायणम् ।\nतं भाषमाणं भगवानुशना प्रत्यभाषत ।\nभीमान्दुष्टप्रलापांस्त्वं तात कस्मात्प्रभाषसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he spoke, reckoned by the count of time and intent on creation and continuance, the blessed Ushanas answered him: \"Dear one, why do you speak such terrible, wrong words?\""}},{"text":"वृत्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vritra said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"प्रत्यक्षमेतद्भवतस्तथान्येषां मनीषिणाम् ।\nमया यज्जयलुब्धेन पुरा तप्तं महत्तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is plain to you and to other wise men: how, greedy for victory, I formerly practiced great austerity."}},{"n":25,"text":"गन्धानादाय भूतानां रसांश्च विविधानपि ।\nअवर्धं त्रीन्समाक्रम्य लोकान्वै स्वेन तेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the scents and many flavors of beings, I grew, overpowering the three worlds with my own power."}},{"n":26,"text":"ज्वालामालापरिक्षिप्तो वैहायसचरस्तथा ।\nअजेयः सर्वभूतानामासं नित्यमपेतभीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wrapped in a garland of flames and moving through the sky, I was invincible to all beings and always without fear."}},{"n":27,"text":"ऐश्वर्यं तपसा प्राप्तं भ्रष्टं तच्च स्वकर्मभिः ।\nधृतिमास्थाय भगवन्न शोचामि ततस्त्वहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lordship won by austerity was lost through my own deeds. Holding to steadiness, lord, I do not grieve for it."}},{"n":28,"text":"युयुत्सता महेन्द्रेण पुरा सार्धं महात्मना ।\nततो मे भगवान्दृष्टो हरिर्नारायणः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I wished to fight the great-souled Mahendra long ago, I then saw the blessed lord Hari Narayana."}},{"n":29,"text":"वैकुण्ठः पुरुषो विष्णुः शुक्लोऽनन्तः सनातनः ।\nमुञ्जकेशो हरिश्मश्रुः सर्वभूतपितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vaikuntha, the Person, Vishnu, white, endless, eternal, with a tuft of munja hair and a golden beard, grandfather of all beings."}},{"n":30,"text":"नूनं तु तस्य तपसः सावशेषं ममास्ति वै ।\nयदहं प्रष्टुमिच्छामि भवन्तं कर्मणः फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely some remainder of my austerity is left, since I wish to ask you about the fruit of action."}},{"n":31,"text":"ऐश्वर्यं वै महद्ब्रह्मन्कस्मिन्वर्णे प्रतिष्ठितम् ।\nनिवर्तते चापि पुनः कथमैश्वर्यमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In what class is great lordship established, brahmin? And how does supreme lordship turn away again?"}},{"n":32,"text":"कस्माद्भूतानि जीवन्ति प्रवर्तन्तेऽथ वा पुनः ।\nकिं वा फलं परं प्राप्य जीवस्तिष्ठति शाश्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From what do beings live, and proceed or return? And what is the highest fruit by which a soul remains eternal?"}},{"n":33,"text":"केन वा कर्मणा शक्यमथ ज्ञानेन केन वा ।\nब्रह्मर्षे तत्फलं प्राप्तुं तन्मे व्याख्यातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"By what action, or by what knowledge, can that fruit be gained, brahmin sage? You should explain this to me."}},{"n":34,"text":"इतीदमुक्तः स मुनिस्तदानीं\nप्रत्याह यत्तच्छृणु राजसिंह ।\nमयोच्यमानं पुरुषर्षभ त्व-\nमनन्यचित्तः सह सोदरीयैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, the sage then answered. Listen, lion among kings, to what he said, you best of men, with undistracted mind, together with your brothers."}}]}]}